From: STM32F769 bench <bench@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rt2800usb: shrink the RX queue to 16 entries on noMMU

Each RX queue entry holds a preallocated skb of about 4.3 KB, which
kmalloc rounds to 8 KB: 128 entries pin 1 MB of kernel memory. On the
16 MB STM32F769I-DISCO that leaves no contiguous 256 KB block for exec
once wpa_supplicant is running. 16 entries are enough for this link.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ralink/rt2x00/rt2800usb.c	2026-11-20 08:04:45.884427701 +0000
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ralink/rt2x00/rt2800usb.c	2026-11-20 08:04:45.901433161 +0000
@@ -719,7 +719,13 @@
 
 	switch (queue->qid) {
 	case QID_RX:
-		queue->limit = 128;
+		/*
+		 * Every RX entry keeps a preallocated ~4.3 KB skb, which lands in
+		 * an 8 KB slab: 128 entries pin 1 MB. On a 16 MB noMMU STM32F7
+		 * that memory, scattered in 8 KB pieces, is what every exec needs
+		 * as one contiguous block. 16 entries keep 128 KB.
+		 */
+		queue->limit = 16;
 		queue->data_size = AGGREGATION_SIZE;
 		queue->desc_size = RXINFO_DESC_SIZE;
 		queue->winfo_size = rxwi_size;
